{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.046,
            0.367,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.088,
            0.835,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": "？ Arrange the following lengths in increasing order: $4   \\frac { 1 } { 1 0 } , \\frac { 4 } { 1 0 } , \\frac { 4 1 } { 1 0 } , 4 1   \\frac { 1 } { 1 0 } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.135,
            0.848,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "? Sonu is measuring some of his body parts. The length of Sonu’s lower arm is $2 \\; \\frac { 7 } { 1 0 }$ units, and that of his upper arm is $^ { 3 } \\frac { 6 } { 1 0 }$ units. What is the total length of his arm?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.221,
            0.847,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": "To get the total length, let us see the lower and upper arm length as 2 units and 7 one-tenths, and 3 units and 6 one-tenths, respectively."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.259,
            0.847,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": "So, there are (2 + 3) units and $( 7 \\pm 6 )$ one-tenths. Together, they make 5 units and 13 one-tenths. But 13 one-tenths is 1 unit and 3 one-tenths. So, the total length is 6 units and 3 one-tenths."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.318,
            0.644,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2+3\\right)+\\left(\\frac{7}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}\\right) \\\\&=(2+3)+\\left(\\frac{13}{10}\\right) \\\\&=5+\\frac{13}{10} \\\\&=5+\\frac{10}{10}+\\frac{3}{10}=5+1+\\frac{3}{10} \\\\&=6+\\frac{3}{10} \\\\&=6\\frac{3}{10} \\\\&=2\\end{aligned}\\tag{a}",
          "image_source": "images/page_4_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.587,
            0.217,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "(b)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.572,
            0.494,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}& 一  \\quad 2 \\quad \\frac{7}{10}  乙  \\\\&\\quad + 3 \\quad \\frac{6}{10} \\\\&\\quad = \\quad 5 \\quad \\frac{13}{10} \\\\&\\quad = \\quad 6 \\quad \\frac{3}{10}\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_4_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.762,
            0.78,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": "Or, both the lengths can be converted to tenths and then added:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.786,
            0.709,
            0.806
          ],
          "content": "(c) 27 one-tenths and 36 one-tenths is 63 one-tenths"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.437,
            0.821,
            0.562,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{27}{10} + \\frac{36}{10} = \\frac{63}{10}",
          "image_source": "images/page_4_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.863,
            0.848,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": "$\\frac { 6 3 } { 1 0 }$ is the same as 60 one-tenths $\\left( { \\frac { 6 0 } { 1 0 } } \\right)$ and 3 one-tenths $\\left( { \\frac { 3 } { 1 0 } } \\right)$ , which is"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.938,
            0.186,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": "50"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
